# NestJS Conventions

## Naming
- Files: kebab-case with role suffix (`*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `*.module.ts`, `*.dto.ts`, `*.guard.ts`)
- Classes: PascalCase; methods/vars: camelCase; env: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`

## Structure
- Feature module owns controller/service/DTO; shared logic goes in `libs/*` and is re-exported via `src/index.ts`
- Prefer constructor injection; avoid `new` for Nest providers
- Use existing interceptors/filters/pipes from `@nestlancer/common` instead of one-off error shapes

## Style
- Strict TypeScript (`tsconfig.base.json`); no `any` unless unavoidable and localized
- ESLint import order: builtin → external (`@nestjs/*` first) → internal (`@nestlancer/*`) → relative → type
- Prettier: single quotes, semicolons, trailing commas, 2 spaces, 100 cols
- Conventional commits: `type(scope): subject` (lowercase subject)
